DESCRIPTION Discovery band: enumerate the Job and CronJob surface and report last-run status honestly.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List the CronJobs and recent Jobs in the cluster, and note any that failed on their last run."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic, drift-tolerant ground truth: the answer addresses CronJobs. Do NOT require "indexer" - the resume/indexer Jobs are EPHEMERAL (they exist only while a re-index runs). Do NOT forbid "Failed": an older CronJob run really failed, so a correct answer may say so; invented failures are the judge's to catch.
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "CronJob")

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The cluster runs two CronJobs, olabs-status/olabs-status-changed and olabs-status/olabs-status-weekly, and both succeeded on their most recent run; one older run of olabs-status-changed (Job olabs-status-changed-29825640) failed. The other Jobs are completed one-off Jobs (such as kubemoot/kubemoot-operator-nats-bootstrap, nats/reprojob, and olabs-status verification Jobs, plus resume/indexer Jobs while a re-index runs). A correct answer lists the real CronJobs with their last-run status, says none failed on its last run, and may note the older failed run; it never invents CronJobs or failures (the set may drift; the constant is reporting only the real discovered Jobs and CronJobs and each one's actual last-run status).")
